  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Phillips 66 has $582M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Phillips 66 has 460 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.3M, and obligations are down 9.1% year over year. Phillips 66 moved up and down across fiscal years, with prior-year obligations of $329M in FY21, $434M in FY22, $479M in FY23, $443M in FY24, and $640M in FY25. Phillips 66 shows the largest single-year total in the available series in FY25 at $640M followed by the current FY26 total of $582M. Phillips 66’s current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations. Phillips 66 recorded year-over-year contraction rather than expansion for the current fiscal period, driven by the difference between FY25 and FY26 totals. Phillips 66’s award count and average award size indicate a mix of many mid-sized awards rather than a few very large grants. Phillips 66’s obligation pattern across six fiscal years gives a short-term view of federal purchasing activity with the company.",
